A man who was suffering from a skin disease came to Jesus. On his knees, he begged Jesus. "If you are willing," he said, "to make me 'clean,' then you can."
Jesus was filled with deep profound anxiety. He reached out and touched the man. He said, "I am ready to do that! Be 'clean'!"
Immediately, the disease left his body. He was cured.
Jesus immediately sent his servant away. And he gave the man a strong warning.
He said, "Don't tell anyone about this. Go and present yourself to the priests. Make the sacrifices that Moses commanded. He will be a witness to the priests and their families that you are 'pure'."
But the man went out and began to speak at once. And he reported the news everywhere. So Jesus could no longer enter a town openly. But he remained in secluded places. Yet people still came to him from everywhere.
Jesus heals a man who could not walk.
After a few days, Jesus entered Cana again. The people heard that he had returned to his house.
