One Sabbath Jesus was walking with his disciples in the wheat fields. The disciples began to pluck heads of wheat.
The Pharisees said to Jesus, "Look! This man is doing what is unlawful on the Sabbath. Why then do your disciples do what is unlawful on the Sabbath?"
He answered, "Have you never heard what David did? He and his companions were hungry. They were in desperate need of food."
That was when my father Abiatar was a great priest. David entered the house of God and ate the bread of the presence, which was only for the priests to eat. David also gave some of it to his men.
Jesus said to them, "The Sabbath was made for man's sake, not man for the Sabbath's sake."
