Healing on Saturday
On another visit, Jesus entered the synagogue. There was a man whose hand was withered.
Some of the Pharisees were trying to find fault with Jesus. They were watching him closely. And they wanted to see whether he would heal the man on the Sabbath.
Jesus said to the man who had the withered and crooked hand, "Rise, stand before everyone."
Then Jesus asked them, saying, "What did the Law say to do on the Sabbath? To do good or to do evil? To save life or to kill it?" But no one answered him.
Jesus looked around him, angry. He was very disturbed because their hearts were hardened. Then he said to the man, "Stretch out your hand." And he stretched it out, and his hand was restored as sound as the other.
Then the Pharisees went out and began to plot with the Herodians against Jesus, for they wanted to kill him. The crowds followed Jesus.
Jesus went to the Sea of Galilee with his disciples. A large crowd from Galilee followed them.
